name air-eagle-sparrow
timeout 300

# THE SAME AEROPLANE, THE OTHER ROUND — and it is the whole reason `f15c` is in the catalogue
# (core/FBAircraft.h): with AIM-7 an F-15C fights the MiG-29's BOUND fight, with AIM-120 it fights the
# F-16's. Byte for byte the geometry of air-eagle-amraam.fbm; the only difference between the two files
# is the four `set store` lines, so every difference in the two telemetry files is the ROUND.
#
# WHAT BINDING IS, mechanically and without one line written for it: FBSeekerHandoverS returns -1 for a
# semi-active seeker, so the fire control publishes fc_tta_s = -1, weapons/FBStoresSystem keeps
# radiating the midcourse uplink for as long as its own target estimate is valid, and pilot/FBEngagement
# measures the support window as the WHOLE predicted time of flight instead of the run to an activation
# ring. FBAirPilot::SupportInhibitsDefend then reports that from the round actually in the air, which is
# why the same airframe answers the question differently with a different loadout.
#
# MEASURED 2026-07-29, against air-eagle-amraam.fbm on the identical geometry:
#
#   | quantity                     | AIM-120 (free)      | AIM-7 (bound)        |
#   | shot                         | t = 216.3 s, 25.4 km| t = 191.3 s, 34.8 km |
#   | ttaS in `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION`| 8.25 s              | -1 (never lets go)   |
#   | seeker                       | active at t = 225.0 | semi-active at launch|
#   | shooter tied to the target   | 8.6 s               | 39.2 s, to impact    |
#   | detonation                   | t = 244.2, miss 0.91 m | t = 230.6, miss 1.72 m |
#
# THE OTHER HALF OF THE PAIR — WHAT HAPPENS WHEN THE SUPPORT BREAKS — is air-bomber-intercept.fbm: a
# MiG-23 fires the same class of round (R-24R, SARH), loses the illumination at t = 212.3 s with 9.9 s
# of flight still to run, and the round arrives at nothing.
#
# READING RULE: exit 1 is the PASS and the FAIL must be `bear`'s. `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION ... ttaS=-1`
# followed by a detonation and NO `missile ILLUMINATION_LOST` line is the statement this file makes: the
# shooter paid for the shot by holding its nose on the target for the whole time of flight.

unit eagle
  team hostile
  module f15c
  spawn 46.90000 6.20000 9000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 90 90 9000            # the controller's call: bearing 090, 90 km, co-altitude
  set store 1 aim7
  set store 2 aim7
  set store 3 aim7
  set store 4 aim7
  set brief_master_arm arm
  wp 46.90000 7.90000 9000 480

unit bear
  team friendly
  module tu95
  spawn 46.90000 7.70000 9000 270.0 380
  wp 46.90000 5.90000 9000 380
  objective survive
